practiceProblems.description:
Rust has a for loop that is used to iterate over the elements of a collection, like an array, in sequence.

      syntax -   for variable in collection {
                    // code block to be executed
                 }

                 let arr = [10, 20, 30, 40, 50];
                 for i in &arr {
                     println!("{}", i);
                 }

Here, i holds the value of each element of the array one by one.

### Task
Write a program which does the following
- Create an integer array $num$ which has the integers - 10, 20, 30, 40, 50, 60, 70, 80
- Output to the console the following
  - All the elements of the given array in separate lines
  - Use the "**for each**" loop syntax defined above

